'''Kinrei-tsuka Kofun''' (金鈴塚古墳) is a {{ill|keyhole-shaped kofun|ja|前方後円墳|1=Zenpokoenfun|1=Zenpokoenfun|12=draft}} located in Nagazuka, {{ill|Kisarazu, Chiba|ja|木更津市|12=draft}}, {{ill|Chiba Prefecture|ja|千葉県|12=draft}}, and is part of the {{ill|Gion-Nagazuka Kofun Group|ja|祇園・長須賀古墳群|12=draft}}<ref>The Gion-Nagazuka Kofun Group is also referred to as the Gion Kofun Group or the Kisarazu Kofun Group. This article adopts the terminology used by Shiraishi (2007) and Ozawa (2007).</ref>.

== Overview ==
