'''Kinrei-tsuka Kofun''' (金鈴塚古墳) is a {{ill|keyhole-shaped kofun|ja|前方後円墳|lt=Zenpokoenfun|1=Zenpokoenfun|comment=doing this because I need to differentiate it in piped links too with my new interwiki tool as not the ambiguous phrase keyhole shaped kofun|1=Zenpokoenfun|1=Zenpokoenfun|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/keyhole-shaped kofun|13=User:Immanuelle/Zenpokoenfun|qq=}} located in Nagazuka, {{ill|Kisarazu, Chiba|ja|木更津市|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kisarazu, Chiba|qq=}}, {{ill|Chiba Prefecture|ja|千葉県|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Chiba Prefecture|qq=}}, and is part of the {{ill|Gion-Nagazuka Kofun Group|ja|祇園・長須賀古墳群|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Gion-Nagazuka Kofun Group|qq=}}<ref>The Gion-Nagazuka Kofun Group is also referred to as the Gion Kofun Group or the Kisarazu Kofun Group. This article adopts the terminology used by Shiraishi (2007) and Ozawa (2007).</ref>.

== Overview ==
{{Japanese Kofun
|name = Kinreizuka Kofun
